NUM-31: spread routed outfall volume over the runoff step it is applied in

assembleRunon() turned the volume an outfall routed onto a subcatchment into
a rate with the PREVIOUS runoff step's span. The rate is then applied over
the runoff step about to be taken, which can be much longer (WET_STEP ->
DRY_STEP) or shorter, while the mass balance books the volume. The
subcatchment therefore received vol x newStep / oldStep. assembleRunon() was
also called before the new step was known; call it once the step is chosen
and clamped to the end of the run, and divide by that step (the same result
as the 5.3.0 patch). With a USE RUNOFF interface file the call is now
skipped, as legacy skips runoff_getOutfallRunon() in that mode.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-31_swmm600.patch

